{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games","id":1136684,"title":"[2E Hack] No Instant Casting \u2013 For Crossover games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-02T12:45:33-07:00","id":1136684,"title":"[2E Hack] No Instant Casting \u2013 For Crossover games","content":"Idea I got from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1135965-do-mages-need-a-bit-of-a-nerf-to-bring-them-in-line\">this topic</a> \u2013 <b>Hack on 2E Mage where you take out Instant Casting, completely.</b> <b>It\u2019s made mostly to even crossover games with other monster splats</b>, but it could also work if you want to run with much more \u2018mages-as-researches\u2019 idea. Still, it will need some changes to the parts of the game so here is topic for that.<br /> <br /> Opening problems with No Instant Casting Hack repercussions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><i>Hung Spell</i> from Time 2 seems to bypass it \u2013 you simply do D&amp;D like \u2018spell preparation\u2019 of rituals in advance. Myself, I think it\u2019s much less as a problem, because to have prepare spells with with Time 2, <b>you still need to cast them in ritual in advance </b>\u2013 and there is limited spells you can have over yourself, in the end.</li> <li><b><i>Adamantine Hand </i>Merit is made obsolete by this Hack in the way it\u2019s now written.</b> Maybe to solve this with No Instant Casting it is to make Merit the way as <i>another </i>Hung Spells without Time 2 where Arrows can channel by their moves the spells they prepared before?</li> </ol><b>Notice:</b> If you think that Awakened have the powerlevel left as it is in 2E corebook when playing with other splats - it's clearly topic not for you, so better leave before making unnecessary bad blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-02-2017, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T12:51:46-07:00","id":1136686,"title":"","content":"A less severe alternative would be to require 1 Reach per dot of Arcana in the spell for instant casting. Keeps the simple stuff instant-able, but anything more than apprentice level or so would cause nearly suicidal levels of Paradox.<br /> <br /> Potentially couple this with the inability to contain Paradox for extra fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T12:53:23-07:00","id":1136688,"title":"","content":"I'd deliberately have a few ways around it. Time 2's Hung Spell, yeah. I'd enable Praxis spells to be instant (instead of their usual benefit). Maybe allow certain Yantras to speed up spell casting to certain semioticly linked spells.<br /> <br /> Ritual casting would still be the norm, but there would be certain ways and circumstances you can get your typical Mage Duel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-02-2017, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T12:58:49-07:00","id":1136692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1136686#post1136686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A less severe alternative would be to require 1 Reach per dot of Arcana in the spell for instant casting. Keeps the simple stuff instant-able, but anything more than apprentice level or so would cause nearly suicidal levels of Paradox.<br /> <br /> Potentially couple this with the inability to contain Paradox for extra fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>And/Or what about 1 Yantra bonus per dot of the Spell? Makes having the right items or circumstances really important. A magical tool lets you use the simple spells, sacraments become far more useful, and prepping the battlefield with the right environments becomes near life-or-death. The Muldra Yantra of Rotes becomes near the only way to get Master-level spells off in one Turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-02-2017, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T13:21:50-07:00","id":1136701,"title":"","content":"Or you can just give him high dots in occult and academics, coupled with a smart phone with Wi-Fi access and a large online library.<br /> <br /> Mage: \u200b&quot;Give me 3 hours and I can ritually cast an unveiling spell to find out...&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200bCell Phone Guy: &quot;Don't bother, I already Googled it and the answer is...&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bTake away instant casting, leaving only ritual, and until the Mage is god like in power he's the dead weight guy that Vampires kick around for...kicks.<br /> \u200bIf the goal is just to limit the Mage's versatility, making him more like the Vampire, than you could limit instant casting to only Rotes &amp; Praxis. That way he has a limited number of 'Disciplines' he can use in the moment while still leaving the potential for ritual casting things when time doesn't matter.<br /> It would make the Mage weaker than Vampires though, most Disciplines have constant costless effects where spells don't.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf the goal is just to nerf Mages so Vampire/Werewolf/Hunter players will be happy that would probably do it and still leave the Mage a playable option.<br /> You could also just go back to playing D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> My intent isn't to be confrontational, just pointing out that Mage versatility is what sets CoD apart from traditional Wizard games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 09-02-2017, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T14:23:03-07:00","id":1136715,"title":"","content":"I like the idea mentioned of doing this but allowing Praxes to be instant cast, letting that become their 'thing'. Makes mages more apt to actually buy a decent handful of them, and still makes them rather versatile but mostly in regards to preparation-based circumstances.<br /> <br /> One suggestion though would be to make ritual times go down a step. IE 1 hour at gnosis 1-2 instead of 3-4, etc. Since they'll be so much more reliant on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T14:56:05-07:00","id":1136721,"title":"","content":"Thirding the &quot;praxes can be instant&quot; idea. Maybe rotes too. And of course legacy attainments. <br /> <br /> Basically just give mages a small arsenal of purchased instant effects, and leave the more flexible improvised stuff to the long rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T16:35:34-07:00","id":1136747,"title":"","content":"Are you serious, It would take 3 hours at Gnosis 1 or 2 to cast a spell in combat, I don't thing anyone will fall for the old &quot;Wait for it, just Wait for it&quot; gag. And while you are casting a spell for 3 hour 86 year old grandma is beating you to death with her cane. Mages are normal without magic. I thought the idea was to reduce them not handicap them. And before you say then do not go into battle before you have prepared the spells you need, you don't always have the choice. You can kiss all direct damage spells goodbye. Protection spells goodbye. This is not a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T16:57:09-07:00","id":1136756,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a flat ban on instant casting strikes me as a bad idea. Your punishing players by making playing a mage much less fun without really achieving your ends of &quot;balance.&quot; Indeed it strikes me that what your actually doing is incentivising some of the more &quot;broken&quot; tricks in a Mages playbook, namely setting up powerful long term buffs of the nature that no other Splat can really compare to. Tell me my Gnosis 2 Mastigos can't cast on the fly, and I will just throw on a daylong Incognito Presence instead, then proceed to murder everyone while they fail to recognise my existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T17:16:16-07:00","id":1136761,"title":"","content":"Oh, there's another thing that needs to be addressed. The Time 4 attainment lets you spend mana instead of reach for instant casting. Even with the &quot;purchased instant&quot; tweak that's going to be severely underpowered compared to the others, and without it it'll be outright useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T21:42:25-07:00","id":1136825,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6084\" data-vbnamecard=\"6084\">2ptTakrill</a> this is topic on Hack of the game \u2013 if you not agreeing with it\u2019s POINT \u2013 \u2018Making No Instant Casting balancing factor in crossovers\u2019 \u2013 it\u2019s better if you leave discussion, because:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It\u2019s a Hack, if you do not like even basic idea of it \u2013 don\u2019t use it, play vanilla game.</li> <li>Saying \u2018you should never, ever do it\u2019 is thread-crapping \u2013 this topic is to hammer details for people WANTING to limit Instant Castings for crossover plays. If you are not agreeing with that statement, you know where topic exit is.</li> </ol>On the other hand, CONSTRUCTIVE criticism is more than welcome. Like I will answer one just right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-03-2017, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T22:03:33-07:00","id":1136832,"title":"","content":"Answering some points raised:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Probably leaving Praxis as only Instant Casting is good idea</b> \u2013 it would make them more sought out and not really breaking more mages than vampires are with their Disciplines chains. <b>Interesting would also to leave as Instants the Legacy Attainments </b>\u2013 then Praxis and Legacy would become REALLY big thing in game and mages would work much more like typical monsters from other splats \u2013 which is kind of point of this very topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li><b>I would miss the Rotes on Instant Casting </b>\u2013 their \u2018you cast as Master of Arcana\u2019 thing is enough to make them working and interesting. Adding Instant Casting in mostly non-Instant setting would return us to classical Mage 2E situation that Rotes are more interesting than Praxes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li><b>No combat magic because of no Instants &amp; Adamantine Hand Merit </b>\u2013 Yes, it\u2019s a kind of point. I was thinking about letting easier Imbuing Items for storing spells to combat applications, but each combat spells you should cast ritually \u2018in a free time\u2019. This would also solve our <i>Adamantine Hand</i> Merit problem, as this Arrows \u2018technique\u2019 would let them to Imbue themselves with combat magic ahead of time. And remember that maybe Fireballs nicely lit your enemies, Sword with +5 Aggravated damage is even more better weapon then.</li> <li><b>Long buffs and \u2018perfect plans\u2019 </b>\u2013 Yes, it\u2019s kind point of Hack to make mages prepare their rituals and \u2018sitting\u2019 on them. If you spend one day on ritual Incognito Presence to kill everyone, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a> , in this time werewolves packs can 3 times raid your Sanctum or kidnap your close ones. It\u2019s kind a point of this Hack idea. Remember, mages are planners in this take, other splats are monkey wrenches that will disrupts his plans.</li> <li><b>Time 4 Attainment </b>\u2013 Was there some ideas for \u2018needed\u2019 Time Attainment that did not got in to book? Something about dodging maybe?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T00:52:08-07:00","id":1136855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1136832#post1136832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Answering some points raised:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Probably leaving Praxis as only Instant Casting is good idea</b> \u2013 it would make them more sought out and not really breaking more mages than vampires are with their Disciplines chains. <b>Interesting would also to leave as Instants the Legacy Attainments </b>\u2013 then Praxis and Legacy would become REALLY big thing in game and mages would work much more like typical monsters from other splats \u2013 which is kind of point of this very topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li><b>No combat magic because of no Instants &amp; Adamantine Hand Merit </b>\u2013 Yes, it\u2019s a kind of point. I was thinking about letting easier Imbuing Items for storing spells to combat applications, but each combat spells you should cast ritually \u2018in a free time\u2019. This would also solve our <i>Adamantine Hand</i> Merit problem, as this Arrows \u2018technique\u2019 would let them to Imbue themselves with combat magic ahead of time. And remember that maybe Fireballs nicely lit your enemies, Sword with +5 Aggravated damage is even more better weapon then.</li> <li><b>Long buffs and \u2018perfect plans\u2019 </b>\u2013 Yes, it\u2019s kind point of Hack to make mages prepare their rituals and \u2018sitting\u2019 on them. If you spend one day on ritual Incognito Presence to kill everyone, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a> , in this time werewolves packs can 3 times raid your Sanctum or kidnap your close ones. It\u2019s kind a point of this Hack idea. Remember, mages are planners in this take, other splats are monkey wrenches that will disrupts his plans.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Praxis and Legacy Attainments as instant casts is the only attractive thing about this setup.<br /> <br /> I kind of agree with Katana. You're incentivising the old &quot;ritual to win&quot; stuff. If your rebuttal is &quot;other splats can just destroy you while you're using your rituals,&quot; then what option do mages have? It's either ritual or nothing. ST basically grants you permission to cast a ritual and if he thinks it is going to be too OP he just throws a supernatural through the window to stop you.<br /> <br /> <br /> I understand the intent, but I'm not seeing why you wouldn't just play a merit-based supernatural or Sleepwalker/Proximi. You'd have tons of options and limitations, and technically still be a &quot;mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> If someone picks up Mage the Awakening, why would they want to play Mage the Awakening: With Many Caveats and Restrictions?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sure there are people that would enjoy this, like OP, but this really does feel like a cheeseburger with no cheese. The point being, you mean a hamburger?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I know your point is you can still use the versatile Mage system when casting ritual spells, but you have admitted that a lot of spells that benefit from being cast in the moment fly out the window. Still, you're keeping the ability to manipulate spell factors and whatever, but you also add that it can all be interrupted easily. What's the point of having all the freedom if it can easily be dismantled? Oh, but you can take precautions and prepare and plan! That doesn't do you any good if your preparing and planning for a confrontation needs to include planning and preparing for the planning and preparing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Everyone watch my back while I do stuff! - Or don't!&quot;<br /> &quot;Okay!&quot;<br /> &quot;All right, I'm done. - Or I'm dead!&quot;<br /> <br /> vs.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm just gonna do stuff.&quot;<br /> &quot;Sounds good.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, even though I disagree with it, the Praxis and Legacy Attainments w/ instant cast would warm me up to the idea. I'd probably still rather play a badass merit-based supernatural that could whip my &quot;Mage's&quot; ass in short order.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T01:41:25-07:00","id":1136859,"title":"","content":"If you cannot digest idea of mages being 'super thaumaturgist', this hack is not for you.<br /> <br /> Remember, even with 'No Instant Casting beside Praxis and Attainments' sorcerers are still SUPERB thaumaturgist or medium.<br /> <br /> Second Sight characters: <i>'Oh, I can only cast one of 3 spells I know.'</i><br /> <br /> Awakened on this Hack: '<i>Let me show you all the rituals I know now from Matter or Death Arcana...'</i><br /> <br /> AND still mage would have those special Praxis and Legacy Attainments he specialized with to Instant Cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-03-2017, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T02:16:45-07:00","id":1136861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1136825#post1136825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6084\" data-vbnamecard=\"6084\">2ptTakrill</a> this is topic on Hack of the game \u2013 if you not agreeing with it\u2019s POINT \u2013 \u2018Making No Instant Casting balancing factor in crossovers\u2019 \u2013 it\u2019s better if you leave discussion, because:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It\u2019s a Hack, if you do not like even basic idea of it \u2013 don\u2019t use it, play vanilla game.</li> <li>Saying \u2018you should never, ever do it\u2019 is thread-crapping \u2013 this topic is to hammer details for people WANTING to limit Instant Castings for crossover plays. If you are not agreeing with that statement, you know where topic exit is.</li> </ol>On the other hand, CONSTRUCTIVE criticism is more than welcome. Like I will answer one just right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad I thought you wanted all opinions not just those that agreed with you, The only reason I am in this thread a second time is because YOU messaged me, don't call out my name and I won't be back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T03:00:01-07:00","id":1136866,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd probably never actually use this hack <i>myself. </i>(I very rarely GM, for one thing) I just think it has enough merit to help hash out the repercussions and see what other mechanics need changing in response.<br /> <br /> Now, one of the reasons I thought it should be rotes <i>and </i>praxes was that I felt a small <i>selection </i>of instant effects would work better for a crossover instead of just one at chargen. And also because rotes are where the magic hand gestures fit in and it seemed wrong not to have mages waving their hands and stuff happening, but primarily it was the first thing.<br /> <br /> So, if you are dead-set at keeping rotes ritual only to avoid having them overshadow praxes, I would consider increasing the number of praxes you get per gnosis. Or maybe just starting with two bonus ones. It would make sense for mages in this setting to want to learn them, possibly at the expense of rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 09-03-2017, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T04:09:52-07:00","id":1136882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1136866#post1136866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd probably never actually use this hack <i>myself. </i>(I very rarely GM, for one thing) I just think it has enough merit to help hash out the repercussions and see what other mechanics need changing in response.<br /> <br /> Now, one of the reasons I thought it should be rotes <i>and </i>praxes was that I felt a small <i>selection </i>of instant effects would work better for a crossover instead of just one at chargen. And also because rotes are where the magic hand gestures fit in and it seemed wrong not to have mages waving their hands and stuff happening, but primarily it was the first thing.<br /> <br /> So, if you are dead-set at keeping rotes ritual only to avoid having them overshadow praxes, I would consider increasing the number of praxes you get per gnosis. Or maybe just starting with two bonus ones. It would make sense for mages in this setting to want to learn them, possibly at the expense of rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Would 1 Praxes per Gnosis and Arcana dot be too much in this model? With the Praxis-from-Arcana being limited to a spell from that Arcana?<br /> <br /> Rotes can be combined with Praxes, if I recall. This is another reason to stack.<br /> <br /> Regarding Time 4, if going with Inodiv's suggestion (+1 Reach per spell dot), it still has a place. If you truly wanted to excise the Reach option, Time 4 could either grant Instant casting for 1 Mana per dot, or increase effective Gnosis for Ritual casting time by 1-2 per Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T04:23:10-07:00","id":1136885,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's an idea. We can model it like Blood Sorcery and say that in addition to a free praxis from every dot of gnosis, you get one for each dot of arcarna of a spell <i>from that dot</i>. <br /> <br /> Oh, but the rule is that you <i>can't</i> combine rotes and praxes. You have to pick one or the other if you know a spell as both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T06:42:21-07:00","id":1136918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1136885#post1136885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, but the rule is that you <i>can't</i> combine rotes and praxes. You have to pick one or the other if you know a spell as both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Change that for this Hack, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T08:21:21-07:00","id":1136938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1136918#post1136918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh. Change that for this Hack, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still do not see why we <i>need</i> both Rotes and Praxes to work the same for the Hack - May someone enlighten me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T09:03:18-07:00","id":1136946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1136938#post1136938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still do not see why we <i>need</i> both Rotes and Praxes to work the same for the Hack - May someone enlighten me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mudras are meant to work as mnemonics to compress imagos. To me that sounds like something that should make magic faster rather than more powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T09:49:25-07:00","id":1136951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1136946#post1136946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mudras are meant to work as mnemonics to compress imagos. To me that sounds like something that should make magic faster rather than more powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>By combining, one needs both the Rote and the spell as a Praxis to employ the Rote benefits as an Instant.<br /> <br /> Really, it is just to enable combat Rotes, really. If Praxes are the route to Instant casting, and Rotes can't be combined with Praxes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T11:01:44-07:00","id":1136967,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, I don't see this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1136832#post1136832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding Instant Casting in mostly non-Instant setting would return us to classical Mage 2E situation that Rotes are more interesting than Praxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>as a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T13:19:08-07:00","id":1137007,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd leave the ruling arcana as normal casting, but enforce a requirement of +1 additional reach to instant cast spells for the rest. Reduces versatility without risk, increases cost of non primary spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T14:33:56-07:00","id":1137045,"title":"","content":"No instant casting at all would make the life of young mages vastly different. They can just do a small handful of spells each day and if they don't use these spells to support their lifestyle (because they have no built-in support network like werewolves or the noticable lowered living expenses of vampires), they will have to work a proper job to make money which in turn reduces their time for ritual casting even more. I think in such a world, new mages would most likely work as ritual helpers or do commisioned spellcasting for older, more powerful mages which can get rid of monetary problems much easier. In such a world cabals would be perhaps most of the time a group of students under a single master ...<br /> Not saying that's a bad idea, just that the game would play different.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you don't want &quot;no instant cast at all&quot;, how about making Praxes of your ruling arcana and Attainments instant castable, add a bunch of yantras that allows to instantly cast other spells - maybe without spells of the lesser arcanum - under very specific circumstances and for the cost of +1 reach (one for each order, with Adamantine Hand being the AA one)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T21:29:08-07:00","id":1137187,"title":"","content":"I gave my suggestion of leaving Rotes and Praxes as instant cast, that was going with your attempt to downgrade Mages to make other splats more competitive. After that I just pointed out that since other splat powers now often have secondary, constant, no cost effects and Mages don't (outside of PMS) then you might actually end up making Mages weaker instead of more balanced.<br /> And yes, I did state that personally what you are creating feels too much like D&amp;D wizards to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bI gave the asked for suggestion and then pointed out flaws that might lead away from what many of us enjoy about the game. The intent was that people would then consider and address those issues, not insulting your intent in posting the question.<br /> <br /> I will now point out that Rotes have two advantages over Praxes;<br /> \u200b1-Hides the Nimbus of the caster within the spell's residue.<br /> \u200b2-Allows the caster to utilize more Yantra than his understanding normally allows. Additional Yantra do require additional rounds in casting to add, which kind of makes Rotes a non instant cast so they might not be the game buster you fear. In combat four rounds to cast a spell probably means I've already lost.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you want to preserve the feel of creative casting in the field without over powering the other splats you could just change the time requirement from starting at three hours to something more workable, yet still cut it out of combat and require some forethought to do. For example; instead of just stepping up to the door and using Forces to trip its electronic lock, the Mage now has to fake out the watching guard by pretending to look for his key card for several minutes while he casts the spell.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you ask me the one element of Mages that tends to overpower the other splats is the various Mage Armor attainments, by the time the Mage has four or five dots in an Arcanum it almost guarantees most opponents will be reduced to a luck die when attacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T23:38:48-07:00","id":1137208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1137187#post1137187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will now point out that Rotes have two advantages over Praxes;<br /> \u200b1-Hides the Nimbus of the caster within the spell's residue.<br /> \u200b2-Allows the caster to utilize more Yantra than his understanding normally allows. Additional Yantra do require additional rounds in casting to add, which kind of makes Rotes a non instant cast so they might not be the game buster you fear. In combat four rounds to cast a spell probably means I've already lost.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait no, rotes dont mean more yantras, they probably mean 1 very good mudras yantra though. There main advantage is extra free reach if applic and no mana cost for non ruling spells. Gnosis determines how many yantras you can add to spells not rotes.<br /> <br /> If you are casting a disciple level spell with a rote you are gaining +3 free reach, probably a +4/5 yantra and no mana cost if its no ruling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T01:28:52-07:00","id":1137238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1137208#post1137208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait no, rotes dont mean more yantras, they probably mean 1 very good mudras yantra though. There main advantage is extra free reach if applic and no mana cost for non ruling spells. Gnosis determines how many yantras you can add to spells not rotes.<br /> <br /> If you are casting a disciple level spell with a rote you are gaining +3 free reach, probably a +4/5 yantra and no mana cost if its no ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I would strifr from mixing Praxis and Rotes - it simply is 'mega win' button here by combaining Instant Casting ( in largly No Instant Casting setting ) that can give you all the Reaches you need. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Most of the time +3 Reaches is all you really need to do anything in Mage 2E spells ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T11:49:15-07:00","id":1137774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1137238#post1137238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why I would strifr from mixing Praxis and Rotes - it simply is 'mega win' button here by combaining Instant Casting ( in largly No Instant Casting setting ) that can give you all the Reaches you need. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Most of the time +3 Reaches is all you really need to do anything in Mage 2E spells ).</div> </div> </div> </div>You still need to find and &quot;buy&quot; the Rotes. If going with Scaling Reach for Instant Casting, then you would burn those 3 free Reach to make it Instant (unless combined with Praxis).<br /> <br /> Rotes let Mages taste what being a Master is like - there is a place for them. They are hardly &quot;I win&quot; buttons. Don't want too many floating around? Restrict access. It is easier to justify in universe than many other alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T06:28:30-07:00","id":1138002,"title":"","content":"If I wanted to discourage Instant casting in place of Rituals, instead of a blank ban I would just increase the Reach needed to be equal to the dot of the spell, as others already suggested. It scales better, allowing Masters to be able to pull 1-3 Practices on the spot, while leaving most potent 4-5 dots usually cast as rituals, or as dangerous on the spot spells. If this proves too lengty, maybe reduce the Ritual time, so the max is 1 hour instead of 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T09:52:53-07:00","id":1138041,"title":"","content":"The problem with moving 4-5 dot spells from instant casting range is that most of the spells that allow Mages to compete with the other splat's powers are within that range, Mages don't start doing lethal damage until 4 dots not to mention utility spells like teleport and levitation.<br /> \u200bLimiting the number of instant cast spells to a handful chosen by the individual and paid extra for seems like the best way to limit Mage versatility without reducing them to mere mortals.<br /> <br /> \u200bSomeone really needs to play test it and see how it actually works out, sure Mages may still overwhelm the competition or they may turn into meat in funny hats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T15:30:20-07:00","id":1138122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1136747#post1136747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are normal without magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are not talking about Magic, we are talking specifically about Spells.<br /> <br /> Without Spells Mages still have Mage Sight and Pattern Restoration, and lets not forget the wealth of Attainments even if they don't have a Legacy.<br /> <br /> That is FAR above normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T22:43:10-07:00","id":1138219,"title":"","content":"And Gnosis as Supernatural Resistance, let's not forget it. <br /> <br /> Vampire:'I stare in to him and Dominate his will.'<br /> Mage-without-spells:'No, you don't - my Gnosis 4 and Resolve 4 deflects your will!'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T15:33:25-07:00","id":1138418,"title":"","content":"Nope, I'd personally never play in a game with this houserule. You already need to pay a reasonable price to cast magic in combat time (Reach), I see no reason to go further than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T03:58:23-07:00","id":1138542,"title":"","content":"Actually, you pay none. Is one flat Reach that you already get for free, you can cast any spell of your highest Practice on the spot without any issue whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Which gives me another optional houserule, just make free Reach equal to the dots above the required for the spell, so if you have 3 dots and want to cast a 1 dot spell, you get just 2 Free Reach before you have to worry about Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T06:50:08-07:00","id":1138566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1138542#post1138542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, you pay none. Is one flat Reach that you already get for free, you can cast any spell of your highest Practice on the spot without any issue whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Which gives me another optional houserule, just make free Reach equal to the dots above the required for the spell, so if you have 3 dots and want to cast a 1 dot spell, you get just 2 Free Reach before you have to worry about Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting view point, Paradox-Free Reach that covers exactly the same level does seem like a subsidy made to make Instant Casting not really a feature that requires expertise above the base requirement to even cast the spell in the first place. I mean since that subsidy of Paradox-Free Reach could be spent on something else but Instant Casting is most obvious first choice of where to spend Reach, it seems to be you have to sacrifice Instant Casting to use that reach on something else, which has the presupposition that somehow something which is listed as an auxiliary effect requiring extra effort is a base entitlement that can be sold for shiny alternative effects.<br /> <br /> I agree the price of 1 Paradox-Free Reach would be a fair price if you had to earn that Reach via having greater mastery, as suggested.<br /> <br /> At the top end of the standard powerscale that's mean even Masters couldn't has Making or Unmaking spells as Instant Casts without risking Paradox and that seems fine given how powerful Making and Unmaking spells are.<br /> <br /> Also it seems odd that a game with a major theme of Hubris would rob its PCs of the common temptation to Reach with the risk of Paradox,and what is more tempting that using your most powerful abilities at the snap of a finger? That's an expression of the dangers of Hubris in mechanical form.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1138576#post1138576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that is a cost. You get Reach for meeting the spell requirement that can be spent on anything. Instead of spending it on something else, you can choose to spend it casting in combat time.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I said, but I was agreeing with how right <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> was. We're looking at the same facts and coming up with different conclusions, likely caused by unaligned paradigms. I like increased risk of Paradox, reducing Paradox-Free Reach by 1 does that nicely, and it seems to fit the tempted to have &quot;man's reach exceed his grasp&quot; Hubris themes be integrated in a mechanical way. As I said before having their greatest powers require Reach which is not Paradox-Free to use Instantly is a significant temptation, and puts a sharper contrast on what a Mage <i>could</i> do and what is safe and sane to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-08-2017, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T07:35:30-07:00","id":1138576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1138542#post1138542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, you pay none. Is one flat Reach that you already get for free, you can cast any spell of your highest Practice on the spot without any issue whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Which gives me another optional houserule, just make free Reach equal to the dots above the required for the spell, so if you have 3 dots and want to cast a 1 dot spell, you get just 2 Free Reach before you have to worry about Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is a cost. You get Reach for meeting the spell requirement that can be spent on anything. Instead of spending it on something else, you can choose to spend it casting in combat time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T08:24:40-07:00","id":1138588,"title":"","content":"You called it a reasonable price, I object that is anything other than a very minor annoyance, most of the time. <br /> <br /> For most spells there's hardly anything that would be a more cost efficient use of that free Reach. Where's the cost of opportunity then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T08:55:26-07:00","id":1138595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1138588#post1138588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You called it a reasonable price, I object that is anything other than a very minor annoyance, most of the time.<br /> <br /> For most spells there's hardly anything that would be a more cost efficient use of that free Reach. Where's the cost of opportunity then?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a reasonable price. You are giving up the ability to spend that reach on something else in order to cast quickly. Sometimes you might want to take your time to cast ritually and take more time to get more dice to pull off something big. In combat where your options are a bit more restricted casting quickly is generally your best course of action, but that doesn't stop it from requiring you to pay a limited resource in order to gain the effect you're wanting, even if that effect is what you believe to be one most necessary for your situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T23:56:28-07:00","id":1138815,"title":"","content":"Let's agree to disagree? I just cannot see as cost something you are given for free, that's all. If you did have to choose between casting Instant or without risking Paradox I would concede your point, but the game is made so that's not really an issue. They could've just made Instant the default and give an extra Reach for casting in Ritual time, it would be mechanically the same but it would've seem not worth it, and that's my point, really, you should see the default as default, but you don't, do you? That free Reach make the whole thing about Ritual magic being the default, absolutely pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T00:33:37-07:00","id":1138822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136684-2e-hack-no-instant-casting-\u2013-for-crossover-games?p=1138815#post1138815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's agree to disagree? I just cannot see as cost something you are given for free, that's all. If you did have to choose between casting Instant or without risking Paradox I would concede your point, but the game is made so that's not really an issue. They could've just made Instant the default and give an extra Reach for casting in Ritual time, it would be mechanically the same but it would've seem not worth it, and that's my point, really, you should see the default as default, but you don't, do you? That free Reach make the whole thing about Ritual magic being the default, absolutely pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I specifically <i>do</i> see the default as the default. The default is ritual casting. <i>That is the default.</i> And for the price of 1 Reach, which you could have used on anything, you can instead choose to change the default speed and cast in combat time instead. If the default was that you automatically cast at combat speed but could gain a Reach if you chose to cast in ritual time <i>then</i> I'd likely concede the point, but it isn't. That said, I will agree to disagree because I don't think it likely that you are going to change your opinion on the matter, and arguing it any further seems rather pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T10:16:07-07:00","id":1138924,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, that first free reach can be seen as going one of two places. Either you're using it to cast a short term spell instantly, <i>or</i> you're using it to make a ritual spell last for a long time. Ideally, longer than it took to cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}